    "available_at": "2026-10-16T10:15:13.101147+00:00",
    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\n2027 BMW F 450 RR Is Like a Mini S 1000 RR, Cheaper Than Therapy\n44 photos\nPhoto: BMW\nIt’s almost EICMA time and, as arguably the largest motorcycle show in the world is approaching, bike makers around the world are waking up following the slow summer months. So did BMW this week, which presented to the world something that’s basically a mini S 1000 RR, available at a fraction of the cost.\nThe name of the new motorcycle is F 450 RR , and it launches in the U.S. as a 2027 model year ride that’s set to become the entry-level machine in BMW’s supersport bikes portfolio, in all the ways that matter, from performance levels to cost.\nThe bike was constructed by the Bavarians around a welded tubular steel space-frame selected to provide the required rigidity. The chassis incorporates forged components, with the engine included in the design as a load-bearing element.\nSpeaking of that, the motorcycle is animated by a liquid-cooled 420cc parallel-twin engine with a 72 mm bore and 51.6 mm stroke. It’s the unit that has already been introduced on the BMW F 450 GS, only reengineered to suit the needs of a supersport.\nThe performance numbers of the transversely mounted piece of hardware are exactly what you’d expect from an entry-level machine: 48 hp at 8,750 rpm and 32 lb.-ft. of torque at 6,750 rpm. These translate into an acceleration time from standstill to 62 mph of 5.6 seconds, and a top speed of 110 mph (177 kph).\nPhoto: BMW Motorrad A stainless-steel exhaust system helps it breathe, and the German bike maker’s Easy Ride Clutch can be on deck to allow riders to enjoy their trip without using the clutch lever. Another component of the drivetrain is the six-speed transmission that sends torque to the left-side secondary drive. The unit comes with a reversible shift pattern suited for use on the track.\nThe motorcycle can be set to operate in one of three main modes, namely Rain, Road, and Race. A series of assistance features are on deck to help riders along, including ABS Pro, Dynamic Brake Control (DBC), and Dynamic Traction Control (DTC).\nBMW Motorrad didn’t cut corners when it comes to the suspension setup either, and it chose KYB components. The company went for an upside-down telescopic fork at the front, adjustable for compression and rebound, and an aluminum hollow-cast double-sided swingarm with a central spring shock at the rear, it too adjustable for spring preload and rebound damping.\nOverall, the bike comes with suspension travel of 5.5 inches. These elements tie into cast-aluminum 17-inch wheels with hollow spokes at both ends. Brembo braking hardware is on deck to supply stopping power.\nPhoto: BMW Motorrad Elsewhere, the 2027 BMW F 450 RR deploys forged-aluminum foot controls and side stand, heated grips right off the factory floor, and footpeg brackets for the passenger that are bolted directly to the frame.\nLast but not least, the motorcycle ships as stock with full LED lights, a 6.5-inch TFT display that allows smartphone connectivity, and a USB-C charging point for the rider’s handheld devices.\nWhen it comes to the overall design, the F 450 RR borrows a lot from its bigger S 1000 RR sibling, including the nose-down/tail-down appearance, the fly line, and winglets. Why, it even comes with an asymmetrical side fairing panel, complete with the telltale gills.\nUp on the frame, BMW installed a 3.69-gallon (14 liters) fuel tank, and behind that a two-piece seat that floats 31.1 inches (790 mm) off the ground. The tail section includes discreetly placed grab handles.\nThe new addition to the BMW supersport motorcycle family may have been presented this week, but it will take a long time to reach the U.S. - the local market won’t see the model become available until the summer of 2027.\nPhoto: BMW Motorrad There will be only one variant available, the M Sport, in a single color choice, Snaefell White / M Motorsport. That means a white frame with wheel decals in the M Motorsport colors, but also that the red version you see in the attached gallery won’t be sold, at least for now, on the American market.\nI said earlier that the 2027 BMW F 450 RR is cheaper than therapy, and it’s about time to reveal what that means. BMW settled on an MSRP of $7,815, making the ride one of the most affordable machines available at the time of writing in BMW’s portfolio.\nThat, of course, is only the starting price, as a lot of extras are on the table, including the $330 Innovation Package, soft cases capable of holding 16.5 liters of stuff, a tank bag , roll bags going from 40 to 60 liters, and so on.\nBMW didn’t specifically say that it will bring the F 450 RR to the Esposizione Internazionale Ciclo Motociclo e Accessori (EICMA) show in Milan, Italy, early next month, but there’s a good chance it will. autoevolution will be on location to bring you all the hot stories from there.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nBMW F 450 RR BMW Motorrad BMW supersport\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Daniel Patrascu\nDaniel loves writing (or so he claims), and he uses this skill to offer readers a \"behind the scenes\" look at the automotive industry. He also enjoys talking about space exploration and robots, because in his view the only way forward for humanity is away from this planet, in metal bodies. Full profile\nUP NEXT Car Nut Got 1968 Charger R/T \"Family Car,\" Bounced 8 States in 32 Years, Broadcast Sheet Still in It",
